select engine_manual_apply(198,'34ea3eea4a10ee633db1a5106e3fb82b',$p$[{"old": "the enforcer model (luna) is an OpenAI model and the panel seats are OpenAI models;", "new": "the enforcer model (luna) is an OpenAI model and the usual panel seats are OpenAI models;"}, {"old": "MiniMax or DeepSeek as either debater (neither debates; md_notes_rulings 421; the enforcer model is luna since ASK 426, §9);", "new": "MiniMax or DeepSeek as either debater (neither debates; md_notes_rulings 421 and ASK 437; the enforcer model is luna since ASK 426, §9); qwen as either debater (out of the debater engines since ASK 437);"}, {"old": "Only a dry regrade takes `rulebook:'draft'`, the test inputs and `qualify_alternate`.", "new": "Only a dry regrade takes `rulebook:'draft'` and the test inputs; `qualify_alternate` is refused in every run since ASK 437."}, {"old": "- JUDGE ORDER AND ALTERNATES, LIVE AS OF ASK 407 (", "new": "- JUDGE ORDER AND ALTERNATES, LIVE AS OF ASK 437 ("}, {"old": "  - Order: Init Seats `ORDER0` and Accept Build `ORDER` are chatgpt, sol, sol62, ember, glm_legal, haiku, hy4, hy4_flash, gemini, hydrogen, spark, qwen4max, argon, sonnet, qwen. `__ALT` is ember, glm_legal, haiku, hy4, hy4_flash, gemini, hydrogen, spark, qwen4max, argon, sonnet: the operator's alternate order of 18 Nov 2026, without 6.1 terra and 6.2 sol, which stay panel seats.", "new": "  - Order: Init Seats `ORDER0` and Accept Build `ORDER` are chatgpt, sol, sol62, haiku, gemini, hydrogen, spark, qwen4max, argon, sonnet. `__ALT` is haiku, gemini, hydrogen, spark, qwen4max, argon, sonnet: the operator's alternate order of 18 Nov 2026 with ember, glm_legal, hy4 and hy4_flash taken out (ASK 437), without 6.1 terra and 6.2 sol, which stay panel seats."}, {"old": "  - New seats (model_config: provider openrouter, role engine, max_tokens 64000, active): glm_legal", "new": "  - Seats added by ASK 407 (model_config: provider openrouter, role engine, max_tokens 64000, active; ASK 437 took glm_legal, hy4 and hy4_flash out of every seat list again): glm_legal"}, {"old": "  - Ember: ember is a seat again, first in the operator's alternate order; the EMBER REMOVED entry above does not describe the live flow.", "new": "  - Removed by ASK 437 (the operator, 21:24 CST on 11-18: flash models and the named models out of debating, judging and the panel; at 21:51 CST he kept Gemini 3.8 Flash and Spark): ember, glm_legal, hy4 and hy4_flash are in no seat list, and qwen is out of the debater engines (`ENG`), so a debate that names qwen as a debater is refused at Init. Their model_config rows are unchanged, and lookup maps (FAM_PANEL, JFAM, ENG_SEAT, Format Markdown's names) still name them but seat no one. DeepSeek's debater refusal reads \"DeepSeek never debates (operator 21:24 CST 11-18): DeepSeek is out of debating, judging and the panel.\" (it gave ruling 421's enforcer reason, untrue since ASK 426). Every `qualify_alternate` is refused: \"qualify_alternate is refused: MiniMax is out of debating, judging and the panel (operator 21:24 CST 11-18).\" That was MiniMax's only way in; `ALT_MODELS` keeps its entries, because emptying it touches model settings.\n  - Live: engine 60bf6007 (from 2d40e6ad), saved 04:27:07Z on 11-19; child unchanged."}, {"old": "  - Shown offline (Init Seats on the stored run 38661 inputs): spark against gemini keeps the panel chatgpt, sol and sol62; the reserve is glm_legal (was haiku); the alternates are glm_legal, haiku, hy4, hy4_flash, qwen4max and sonnet. An OpenAI debater bars all three panel seats, and the panel is drawn from the alternates (glm_legal, haiku and hy4 in those inputs, where ember did not accept the posture).", "new": "  - Shown offline (ASK 437, Init Seats live against target for 132 ordered debater pairs): 0 pairs seat a removed model; 42 pairs are refused (a qwen or DeepSeek debater); in the 72 pairs with no OpenAI debater, the panel and the single judge are unchanged. A dry `qualify_alternate` for MiniMax is refused. An OpenAI debater bars all three panel seats, and the panel is drawn from the alternates."}, {"old": "  - Limits: each new model has one provider on OpenRouter (Z.AI for glm_legal, Tencent for hy4 and hy4_flash, Alibaba for qwen4max), so an outage there leaves only the alternate path. The 900 s rule applies to these seats as to every judge. Not shown by a run.", "new": "  - Limits: qwen4max has one provider on OpenRouter (Alibaba), so an outage there leaves only the alternate path. In the ASK 437 trial the fewest alternates in a pair is 2. The 900 s rule applies to every judge. Not shown by a run; its mark is the first run's Init Seats output and Accept Build seat list holding none of ember, glm_legal, hy4, hy4_flash, qwen, deepseek or MiniMax."}, {"old": "kjv_word_map by strongs_number for glossed numbers (limit 1,000, up to 30 numbers).", "new": "kjv_word_map by strongs_number for glossed numbers (limit 1,000, up to 100 numbers since ASK 438; 30 before)."}, {"old": "  - Limits: Part B misses -ed forms (H2030 \"conceived\" is flagged though the KJV renders \"conceive\"); binding errors", "new": "  - Limits: Part B read no -d or -ed forms until ASK 430 (below); binding errors"}, {"old": "added after today's list only while the list stays within 60 glosses and every number named is among the 30 numbers read,", "new": "added after today's list only while the list stays within GLOSS_CAP glosses and every number named is among the NUM_CAP numbers read (250 and 100 since ASK 438; 60 and 30 before),"}, {"old": "with zeros where no new form occurs.", "new": "with zeros where no new form occurs. Its words \"60-gloss and 30-number caps\" are fixed text in Build Save Body and were not changed by ASK 438, so since then they name the old caps."}, {"old": "  - Limits: the caps are unchanged; raising them is a separate decision. A quote that does not follow at once", "new": "  - Limits: ASK 438 raised the caps (below). A quote that does not follow at once"}, {"old": "The renderings matcher adds -s, -es and -ies but not -d or -ed, so \"prepare\" (KJV \"prepared\") is written NOT IN THE KJV RENDERINGS. The judges'", "new": "Since ASK 430 the renderings matcher also reads -d and -ed forms (below). The judges'"}, {"old": "- INDEX ON kjv_word_map.kjv_word (ASK 343; database only):", "new": "- THE GLOSS TRIAL READS -d AND -ed FORMS, LISTS KJV RENDERINGS BY USE, AND RAISES ITS CAPS (ASK 430, 436 and 438; L2 Count Plan and L2 Gloss Plan; Part B of ASK 340, record-only):\n  - Why: Part B wrote a gloss NOT IN THE KJV RENDERINGS when it differed from a rendering only by -d or -ed (G2675 \"prepare\", KJV \"prepared\", run 39015); the KJV list on a gloss row was the first 24 renderings alphabetically, with no sign of a cut, so H1121 never showed \"son\"; and the caps of 60 glosses and 30 numbers cut glosses in 97 of 240 stored runs (ASK 432), none of the last 8.\n  - What it does: ASK 430: the forms list in L2 Count Plan, which made -s, -es and -ies, also makes -d (a stem of 3 or more letters ending in a single e), -ed, a doubled consonant + -ed and -ied, and strips them back; -ed is stripped only when 3 or more letters stand before it, so \"used\" does not match the KJV \"us\". ASK 436: L2 Count Plan keeps a count per KJV word; the KJV list on a gloss row is ordered by count (ties alphabetical), first 24, then \"and N more\" when cut. ASK 438: in L2 Gloss Plan, GLOSS_CAP=250 and NUM_CAP=100 replace 60 glosses and 30 numbers at the gloss list, the ASK 406 add test and the renderings read. The Part A caps (40 candidates, the counts read's 40) are unchanged.\n  - Reach: record-only. e340.gloss is read only by Build Save Body (AUDIT v57) and Format Markdown; the judges' __GLOSS line is built from tags and the lexicon and is unchanged.\n  - Shown offline: ASK 430, 237 stored runs: 182 rows moved to FOUND in 88 runs, 0 FAIL, each hand-read as the same English word. ASK 436, 237 runs: 6,311 rows changed in 195 runs, only gloss[].kjv. ASK 438, 240 runs: 95 runs gain 3,783 glosses and 700 numbers, 0 cut at the new caps (most in a run: 202 glosses, 73 numbers), today's glosses unchanged at the head. L2 Gloss Read does not send its items one after another (64 items 2,353 ms, 9 items 1,251 ms), so the worst run gains about 1 second.\n  - Live: engine 9a7841f0 (from 60bf6007), saved 04:46:25Z on 11-19; child unchanged.\n  - Limits: not shown by a run. \"need\" against a KJV \"nee\" would match (no stored case). \"and N more\" is text in the list; both readers only join and print it. The AUDIT v57 clause still names the 60-gloss and 30-number caps (ASK 406 entry).\n- INDEX ON kjv_word_map.kjv_word (ASK 343; database only):"}]$p$::jsonb,null,null,null,null,null,false) r;